2007 five and a half years after I got home from Pakistan and more than five years after we started

00:23:10.400 --> 00:23:19.840
torturing Abu Zubaydah I got a call from Brian Ross at ABC News and he said that someone had told him

00:23:19.840 --> 00:23:27.840
a source had told him that I had tortured Abu Zubaydah. I said that was absolutely untrue. I

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:36.320
was the only person who was kind to Abu Zubaydah. I have never raised a hand to a prisoner in my life.

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:42.720
I said your source is either mistaken or he's lying and I came to the conclusion later that the

00:23:42.720 --> 00:23:47.600
source was lying because it turned out the source was at the White House. So I decided

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:54.800
that now was the time to come clean that the American people owned this information. The

00:23:54.800 --> 00:24:00.960
American people had a right to know what their government was doing in their name.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:10.320
Besides the fact that it is illegal it is a felony to classify a crime and what I mean by that is

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:17.920
if you are doing something that is a crime whether in the United States or under international law

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:27.440
it is illegal to make that operation classified. By definition because it's a crime it has to remain

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:34.480
unclassified and so on December 11th 2007 I gave a nationally broadcast interview with Brian Ross

00:24:34.480 --> 00:24:39.680
at ABC News and I said three things that just changed the course of the rest of my life.

00:24:40.320 --> 00:24:45.520
I said that the CIA was torturing its prisoners. I said that torture was official

00:24:45.520 --> 00:24:51.200
US government policy. It was not the result of a rogue CIA officer as President Bush had said

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:57.200
disingenuously and I said that the torture program had been personally approved by the

00:24:57.200 --> 00:25:05.200
president himself. As you might imagine within 24 hours the CIA reported me to the FBI.

00:25:05.200 --> 00:25:10.400
They filed something called a crimes report saying that I had leaked classified information

00:25:10.400 --> 00:25:18.880
to the media. The FBI investigated me for a full year from December of 2007 until December of 2008

00:25:18.880 --> 00:25:24.000
and then they sent my attorney something called a declination letter declining to prosecute me.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:32.480
They said that I had not violated the law. Four weeks later Barack Obama becomes president

00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:38.400
and he appoints John Brennan an old nemesis of mine to be the deputy national security advisor

00:25:38.400 --> 00:25:46.400
for counterterrorism. I had no idea that John Brennan secretly asked the justice department

00:25:46.400 --> 00:25:52.000
to reopen the case against me and so for the next three years my phones were tapped,

00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:58.880
my emails were intercepted and teams of FBI agents followed me not all the time

00:25:59.440 --> 00:26:06.720
but followed me periodically wherever to the grocery store, to church, to a restaurant

00:26:06.720 --> 00:26:13.600
with my family. They followed me to my to my mom's sister's funeral in Ohio. I actually didn't know it

00:26:13.600 --> 00:26:20.800
was them and I reported it to the FBI thinking maybe it's a terrorist, maybe it's a criminal,

00:26:20.800 --> 00:26:30.880
you know who knows. Here it was the FBI and I reported it to the FBI. So in January 2012

00:26:30.880 --> 00:26:39.280
this all came to a head and I was arrested and charged with five felonies including three counts

00:26:39.280 --> 00:26:47.040
of espionage. Now as how we pointed out espionage is one of the gravest crimes with which an American

00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:55.120
can be charged and in many cases it carries with it the death penalty. I knew in my heart

00:26:55.120 --> 00:27:00.640
I hadn't committed espionage talking to ABC News or really talking to the American people

00:27:00.640 --> 00:27:13.440
via ABC News is not espionage and so I hired a team of A-list nationally known national security

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:18.000
attorneys here in Washington and we decided we were going to fight. Now let's talk about that

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:24.320
espionage act for a minute. How we mentioned that the espionage act was was written and

00:27:24.320 --> 00:27:31.680
passed into law in 1917 the stated purpose at the time was to combat German saboteurs during the

00:27:31.680 --> 00:27:38.800
first world war. It was never used against German saboteurs it was used against progressives and

00:27:38.800 --> 00:27:49.760
anti-war activists but between 1917 and 2009 the espionage act was used to prosecute three people

00:27:49.840 --> 00:27:56.720
who had spoken to the media right now how we mentioned correctly that it was used against other

00:27:57.440 --> 00:28:02.800
political opponents of whatever president happened to be in office but three people

00:28:02.800 --> 00:28:10.400
were prosecuted for speaking to the media. Just under Barack Obama eight Americans

00:28:10.400 --> 00:28:16.640
were charged with espionage for speaking to the media. Barack Obama had what I would describe

00:28:16.640 --> 00:28:27.520
as a Nixonian obsession with leaks. The New York Times said that the point of my prosecution

00:28:27.520 --> 00:28:34.160
was not even really to prosecute me it was not even really to punish me it was to frighten

00:28:34.160 --> 00:28:42.080
every other person in the national security apparatus from going to the public from going

00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:49.120
to the press to discuss waste fraud abuse illegality or threats to the public health or public

00:28:49.120 --> 00:28:55.360
safety which is the definition of whistleblowing the legal definition and certainly Scott Shane

00:28:55.360 --> 00:29:01.360
at the New York Times told me that on the day of my arrest every single one of the New York

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:10.480
Times national security sources went silent and stayed silent. It's kind of a long story

00:29:10.480 --> 00:29:14.240
but I'm going to skip a lot of it we could talk about it in the questions and answers

00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:23.280
what ended up happening was this I was facing 45 years in prison in my first meeting with the

00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:28.800
Justice Department that's what they offered me 45 years and one of the Justice Department's

00:29:28.800 --> 00:29:36.320
lawyers said take the plea Mr. Kiriakou and you may live to meet your grandchildren I said

00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:46.640
I'm not doing 45 minutes later on they came down to 10 years on a Monday 10 years they said take a

00:29:46.640 --> 00:29:52.800
guilty plea to espionage and do 10 years I said I didn't commit espionage and I haven't done

00:29:52.800 --> 00:29:59.920
anything to be ashamed of on Wednesday two days later they came down to eight years

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:06.320
years. And then on Friday, they came down to five years. My lead attorney was a giant

00:30:06.320 --> 00:30:14.600
by the name of Plato Kacheris. And Plato said, these were his exact words. I've been a practicing

00:30:14.600 --> 00:30:21.720
attorney in Washington for 52 years. And he said, I've never seen them come down in time.

00:30:21.720 --> 00:30:27.000
He said, usually they'll offer you 10. If you turn it down, they offer you 15.

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:32.040
If you turn it down, they offer you 18. And I said, well, why are they coming down in time

00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:38.000
with me? And very quickly he said, because they have a shit case and they know it's shit.

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:42.240
So I said, well, what do we do? He said, we fight and we go to trial. You didn't do anything

00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:50.280
wrong. The truth of the matter is, according to ProPublica, which did a study published

00:30:50.280 --> 00:30:59.400
in November of 2012, the federal government wins 98.2% of its cases. Almost all of those

00:30:59.400 --> 00:31:05.560
are a result of two techniques that the Justice Department uses. One is called charge stacking,

00:31:05.560 --> 00:31:09.520
and the other is venue shopping. Now venue shopping is easy. They charge you in the

00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:14.440
federal district where you are most likely to be convicted and where you are most

00:31:14.440 --> 00:31:22.520
likely to get a long sentence. That's why I was charged in the eastern district of Virginia.

00:31:22.520 --> 00:31:28.880
It's called the espionage court because no national security defendant has ever won a case there.

00:31:28.880 --> 00:31:33.600
That's where they charged Jeffrey Sterling. That's where they charged Chelsea Manning.

00:31:33.600 --> 00:31:40.120
That's where they charged, well, Chelsea Manning was military, but her contempt was

00:31:40.120 --> 00:31:47.000
eastern district. That's where they charged Ed Snowden and Julian Assange. The other one

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:51.040
I said is charge stacking. So what they'll do is they'll charge you. Let's say maybe

00:31:51.040 --> 00:31:54.920
you did do something wrong, but they won't charge you with one crime. They'll charge

00:31:54.920 --> 00:32:00.080
you with 10, 20 felonies, and they'll wait until you go bankrupt, and then they'll

00:32:00.080 --> 00:32:04.560
come and say, all right, listen, we'll drop all the charges if you plead guilty

00:32:04.640 --> 00:32:11.640
to one felony. Well, what are you going to do? I had five kids at home. I knew that

00:32:11.640 --> 00:32:18.760
they won 98.2% of their cases. I was facing 45 years in prison. They're offering me

00:32:18.760 --> 00:32:23.200
now their final, their best and final offer was two and a half years. I do 23

00:32:23.200 --> 00:32:29.600
months. So I hired OJ Simpson's jury consultant who happened to be the

00:32:29.600 --> 00:32:35.840
uncle of my best friend's wife. Oh, no, eastern district of Virginia is in

00:32:35.840 --> 00:32:41.800
Alexandria, Virginia in response to one of the questions. So I hired the jury

00:32:41.800 --> 00:32:47.160
consultant and he came up and we got him, we got him a security clearance

00:32:47.160 --> 00:32:50.760
because all my lawyers had to be cleared. He went through all 15,000

00:32:50.760 --> 00:32:54.880
pages of discovery. And then we all met in this big conference room and he

00:32:54.920 --> 00:33:01.560
said, if we were in any other district in America, we would win this thing. He

00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:05.840
said, but the eastern district of Virginia, your jury is going to be made up

00:33:05.840 --> 00:33:13.120
of people from the FBI, the CIA, the Pentagon, intelligence community

00:33:13.120 --> 00:33:16.440
contractors and their family members. He said, you don't have a prayer.

00:33:17.120 --> 00:33:21.320
Just take the deal. The night before I had to give the justice

00:33:21.360 --> 00:33:27.680
department an answer, my wife and I stayed up all night long. I was only the

00:33:27.680 --> 00:33:31.560
second American ever charged with violating the Intelligence Identities

00:33:31.560 --> 00:33:39.240
