00:33:39.240 --> 00:33:45.720
were several law review journals from Harvard Law School. And we concluded

00:33:45.720 --> 00:33:50.200
that I just hadn't done anything wrong. I hadn't broken the law. And so I

00:33:50.200 --> 00:33:53.600
came on my attorneys at six o'clock in the morning and I said, I've been

00:33:53.600 --> 00:33:57.800
thinking about it all night and I decided I want to go to trial, thinking

00:33:58.920 --> 00:34:03.520
stupidly that once I got in front of a jury, they would see how ridiculous

00:34:03.520 --> 00:34:07.480
this was. They see that it was political. They would see that I had

00:34:07.480 --> 00:34:12.600
done a public service. And my lawyers called me and said, or one of them

00:34:12.600 --> 00:34:15.400
called me and said, put on a pot of coffee, we're on the way over. They

00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:18.520
came over to my house. They told me, you can't turn this down. You

00:34:18.520 --> 00:34:23.680
have to take the deal. If you're convicted, you're seriously looking

00:34:23.680 --> 00:34:28.560
at 12 to 18 years. Just take the deal. I still didn't want to take the

00:34:28.560 --> 00:34:32.800
